Z||000017||Fiero5||05-09-2001||10:44 AM||||Well, I kinda like it.<BR>Three reasons why: <BR>(1) It certainly doesn't look like anyone elses Fiero.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroDupont.JPG"> <BR>(2) It's the first true race car paint scheme I have seen, and looks like a good job on it too!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroDupontfront.JPG"> <BR>(3) It's a Fiero, so it can't be all bad. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroDupontint.JPG"> <BR>I have seen others color their Fiero interior different colors. Except for the bowtie on the hood, though that is probably what that car is in real life, I think it is awesome! I am not a Jeff Gordon fan (I think his was 24 Dupont, now Pepsi?). If I had the cash, I would seriously consider buying it. You can't tell me that thing doesn't turn some heads going down the street or gather a huge crowd at a show? And that is part of the fun of having a fun car like a Fiero to drive.<P>The owner is probably a fan of Jeff Gordon, and took that to a level to make his/her Fiero unique from everyone else. Can't flame them for that. We can agree not everyone would want to do that to a Fiero, but it is certainly different and unique.<P>Just my 2 cents anyway<P>Steve ||||reg||12
Z||000018||Fiero5||05-09-2001||10:49 AM||||I have another reason to add:<BR>(4) It's a T-Top to boot! Can you say bonus?<P>Granted I wouldn't do that to a rare T-Top Fiero either, as a solid roof or sunroof one would have made more sense. Probably that was what they had at the time when they decided to do this. Doesn't really matter now, it's done and it looks pretty cool I think.<P>Steve||||reg||12
